## 1 · Definition of DEPLOYED (v4)

v4 is **deployed** when every row below reads PASS **in one aggregate run** (`tools/check-deployed`, PROPOSAL; CLAUDE.md §5 "an aggregate refuses as one unit"). Each row prints `D<n> <value> <verdict>`, and the aggregate prints `deployed=N/10 tree=<sha> dirty=0 verdict=`. *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V7 F01)* **Before the tag the aggregate runs over D1–D9 and prints `deployed=N/9`**: D10 is the tag itself, so it cannot be an input to the tag's own entry gate or message. D10 is first measured at P9 entry, where `deployed=N/10` is first printed. A row that looked at nothing is UNMEASURED and counts as red (F138).

*(rev 2026-10-01 final-lessons, S-1 / MM-61 / MM-34 / AP-34 / L-18)* **Only this run prints a D-row.** A D-row value is never copied from an agent receipt, a landing record, a rehearsal note or an earlier run. A report that relays a D-row quotes the `check-deployed` line and its `tree=`. *(rev 2026-10-01 V6-fix)* A committed record that the row itself re-verifies at query time (the D6 host records under the staleness rule, the D7 rehearsal record) is that row's input, not a copy; what is forbidden is quoting its value without the run.
*(rev 2026-10-01 final-lessons, S-4 / MM-59 / AP-26)* **Read-backs parse; they never regex a declaration.** Use `systemctl show -p` key=value output, the manifest through a JSON parser, and `PRAGMA` results. Where a byte census remains (the `seam_strings` count in D1/D2), the row prints its method limit: what the census can over-count and what it can under-count.
*(rev 2026-10-01 final-lessons, MM-31 / MM-39 / AP-22 / CM "a control is evidence about the world it last ran in")* **The aggregate has a control, and the control runs before the aggregate's first real use.** `tools/check-deployed --control` plants one fault per D-row in a disposable HOME, for example a wrong engine digest, a missing socket, or a backup log with no `verdict=` line. It asserts each row's own diagnostic and prints `cases=10/10`. It runs at P7 entry, before the first real `check-deployed`: the first real unit is a world the aggregate has never seen (F115).

Lineage: v3's definitions were HO-01 (DR:522-535), PX-4 (DR:1222: B16 + unit + G11 rehearsal) and S15's three tag preconditions (DR:1702-1707). v4 keeps all of them and adds D5, D7 and D9, which v3 deferred to T18 and never built (A4).

