|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| D1 | **Installed release by digest.** `current` names `releases/<sha256(manifest)>/`. Both binaries' sha256 equal the manifest. `seam_strings=0/0`. The manifest meets every RA7 obligation, including linker, CRT, libgcc and link argv. | `readlink -f ~/.local/lib/hee4/current` *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-11)*; `sha256sum <rel>/{hee4,hee4-namespace-shim}`; `sha256sum <rel>/manifest.json` = dir name; the `hee4 release install` read-back (V4-15; v3 `install-release --verify` shape) prints `release=… engine=… shim=… seam_strings=0/0 current=ok host_readback=ok` (IR:562-564 shape) | host read-back line, quoted whole | the running bytes are a test build, or cannot be identified (FC1:131) | PASS_WITH_GAPS: installed (`current`→`38f3dfd2…`, M-1001), but RA7's "cc" is incomplete (RT §1 corr. 5; DR:1883) |
