| D5 | **Backups and restore drill.** (a) `serve` takes a backup at start and before any dispatch whose last backup is more than 15 min old (CD:72). *(rev 2026-10-01 ratified V4-58, DC-22)* The same CD:72 sentence adds three triggers: quiesce and back up after each task once freshness has expired, at every batch boundary (at most 8 tasks), and before an upgrade. It also forbids a background backup daemon. These are one rule with four triggers, not three rival cadences. The destination is on a **different physical disk** (DR:1800). (b) A **restore drill**: restore the newest backup into a disposable HOME, run `recovery` to `complete`, and compare ledger digest and object count with the source at the backup cutoff. (c) The habitat `hee4-backup.timer` (codebase, evidence, handoffs) is enabled, and its last run reads `verdict=PASS`. | (a) `ls` the backup dir: manifest-last, `objects=<n>` printed with its bound. (b) `hee4 restore --into <disp> <backup-id>` (ULTRAMAP §4a, *rev 2026-10-01, V4-15*) then `health` → `recovery=complete`; line `restore backup=<id> ledger=<d> objects=<n>/<n> rto_s=<t> verdict=PASS`. (c) `systemctl --user is-enabled hee4-backup.timer` and `journalctl --user -u hee4-backup` `verdict=` line (CL § durability says to read the verdict lines, not `LAST`). *(rev 2026-10-01 final-lessons, S-7 / V1 §5 HIGH / AP-29)* The service's exit status is **derived from its own last `verdict=` line**, using the roster's contract: PASS→0, PASS_WITH_GAPS→10, FAIL→20, no line→30. The row reads `systemctl --user show -p Result,ExecMainStatus hee4-backup.service` alongside the verdict line and refuses when they disagree. A job whose exit code is its runtime's rc reads FAIL as success. | host record, restore line with both numbers, RTO measured against CD:73 (≤10 min) | unrecoverable state (DS17, DR:1704) | FAIL: no restore verb (MA row 4, "no restore"). Backup format /1 has a 4096-object ceiling (RT §1). No engine backup dir: `/var/mnt/STORAGE-10TB/herdr-engineering-engine-v3-backups` is absent (M-1001) |
| D6 | **A real task ACCEPTED end to end on the host, through the live GPU model.** It is submitted through the unit's socket, not a transient T3 unit, and goes admit → dispatch → candidate (musl, netns separated) → `native::execute` → check → accept. It includes one fail → repair → verify → accept task (B16 shape). | `hee4 task.get <id>` *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-11)* → `state=accepted`; read-only ledger closure lines (FC1:218-221 shape, extended for repair); `worker_settle` carries `identity_sha256` and usage in one settle (FC2:91-95); the daemon at the endpoint is the pinned exe `12ff8654…`, and the `/api/ps` readback shows `size_vram > 0` (**GPU**, not CPU; the t3a CPU copy timed out, FC2:112-117); R0 netns differs (FC1:203) | ~~committed host record `evidence/host/F06.json` + `F07.json`~~ *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V7 F05)* a committed **P7** host record `evidence/host/F06u.json` (RQ7-r2 kind, DR:1737-1752) made **through the unit's socket**, including the fail → repair → verify → accept task, verified by the scoreboard's recompute. F06/F07 stay P4/P5 exit evidence: they run in a disposable HOME before the unit exists (P6), so they cannot satisfy this row | an unreconciled dispatch or an accepted stale generation on the spine (FC1:258) | PASS_WITH_GAPS: F06 host record t3e held all four lines (DR:1861), but it ran under a **transient** T3 unit in a disposable HOME, and there is no B16/F07 |
| D7 | **Recovery runbook rehearsed by execution.** `runbooks/06-deploy.md` (install → commission → start → submit → stop) and `runbooks/07-recover.md` (restore drill; rollback to the previous release; forward-recover; prune under the 128 GiB budget; release retention) were run step by step, each step with its exit code. *(rev 2026-10-01 final-lessons, CM F132 / AP-49)* 07-recover includes one **real-kill step**: after N `task.submit` calls were acknowledged through the socket, send `kill -KILL <MainPID>`; ~~after the unit restarts,~~ *(rev 2026-10-01 open-tasks CN-06)* then start it explicitly with `systemctl --user start hee4.service` (no `Restart=` is configured anywhere in this atlas, so the step does not rely on one), and `task.list` prints `acked_present=N/N`. The rehearsal record lists the task ids this step submitted, and D9 excludes them, so rehearsal tasks never count as use. Only the real writer under a real kill shows "recorded before the ack" (in v3, a double held the kill test while a buffered writer lost 0/1 … 187/200). | a rehearsal record listing every runbook step with `rc=`, the pre/post `list-units` diff, and the `readlink current` before and after rollback | rehearsal record (G11 kind) | the operator cannot recover what the product cannot | FAIL: `runbooks/04-release-recovery.md` reads "Availability: planned" (v3 tree @b5367bc) |
| D8 | **Every scoreboard flow names its L2 test or a reason**, with host rows verified. | `tools/check-flow-scoreboard` → `flows=N l2=M (host=H) reasoned=R unexplained=0 verdict=PASS` | gate output | a flow asserted only in prose | v3: `flows=20 l2=3 host=1 reasoned=17` (DR:1875) |
| D9 | **Used.** RA9's `use` row counts tasks ACCEPTED through the deployed unit (not T3), and is ≥ 1 at the tag. It is re-measured in every Tier-3 record afterwards. | a ledger query through `task.list state=accepted`, filtered to tasks whose `serve_cgroup` column (written at admission, ULTRAMAP §5a *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-15)*; built in **P2** *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V7 F04)*) ends in `/hee4.service`, excluding the task ids the D7 real-kill step lists in its rehearsal record *(rev 2026-10-01 open-tasks CN-06)* | Tier-3 record row | "deployed" meaning installed but unused (the drought diagnosis at DR:1708) | baseline 0 (DR:1552) |
