## 2 · Phase map

**Protocol per phase** (NW:55-78): flow contract → compiled walking skeleton → at most 2 design rounds → slices with Tier-1 → Tier-2 per stack → Tier-3 per day. **The brake** (CLAUDE.md §1; FINAL:168): every slice names its l2 delta or a written excuse. Two unexcused zero-delta stacks stop the line.

| Phase | Entry gate | Work (slices) | Exit evidence | l2 / precondition moved | Held for Luke | Est. size |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **P0 Scaffold** | Luke says **"start coding"** (DR:1897). The `migrated/` writer has finished (A1: done). *(rev 2026-10-01 final-lessons, S-9 / JEV F-A, F-B)* **The Jev door knows v4 before v4 text exists.** JP0 is applied: the synthetic v4 line → `jev-boundary text` rc=3. Luke has ruled on F-B (JP2). From P0 on, every v4 session writes engine text, and the Stop verifier sent engine report text to Jev on 5 of 5 `block_fail` rows (V2 §1). ~~Entry prints the number of v4-cwd rows the verifier sent after JP0, which must be `0` (H-8).~~ *(rev 2026-10-01 V6-fix)* Entry prints the number of engine-text rows the verifier sent after JP0, which must be `0` (H-8). The count is over **every** sent row, from any cwd: the F-B rows came from cwd `~`, not a v4 cwd (V2 §1), so a v4-cwd filter cannot see the leak it names. Each sent row's claim head is replayed through `jev-boundary text`, and entry prints `sent_engine_rows=0/<sent>`. *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V7 F03, V10 (c))* The count is over **every sender**: the Stop verifier, the router and jev-recall (H-8, which absorbs H-25). jev-recall logs no cwd or session today, so until it writes a countable row per send its count is UNMEASURED, and an UNMEASURED sender keeps entry red. Entry also needs Luke's H-10a ruling on non-ZDR terms. *(rev 2026-10-01 final-lessons, S-6 / L-20 / AP-50)* The §5 grant sweep has been put to Luke, and entry prints `grants_pending=` for the P0 rows. *(rev 2026-10-01 alignment)* Design conflicts to ratify or settle at entry: §9 row P0. *(rev 2026-10-02 V4-74)* **Read back by `just jev-entry`** (`hee4db jev-entry`): the JP0 battery through the real door with the v3 and clean controls, and `sent_engine_rows=E/S` over all four senders (verifier, router, read gate, recall) since the door and its loggers were installed; jev-recall now appends one row per send with its cwd, so no sender is UNMEASURED by design. F-B is ruled YES (V4-73) and enforced. The entry value is the run made at entry, never a