| Disks (M-1001) | `/var/home`: btrfs on LUKS NVMe, **397 G free** (RC01 needs a 96 GiB reserve). `/var/mnt/STORAGE-10TB`: `/dev/sdb1` ext4, **7.6 T free** (256 GiB reserve). These are separate physical disks, as required (DR:1800) | same view of `$HOME`. `/tmp` = **tmpfs, 41 G** (M-1001; 47G on 2026-10-01 08:20, gap review N9 *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V7 F19)*) | — |

### 3.2 Traps, each with its v4 structural answer

| Trap | Source | v4 answer |
|---|---|---|
| The host has no `cc`, so anything that links with the system cc cannot build on the host | DR:1770 | Candidates are musl + rust-lld. The engine and sqlite are built only in the toolbox. The manifest records linker, CRT and link argv (D1) |
| A toolbox-built engine running on the host | HO-01 INTERP (DR:569, :803) | Measured by v3's first host start (t3b passed, FC2:124-126). v4 re-measures at P4, and a glibc mismatch is a stop (FC1:134) |
| v3's code root is invisible from the toolbox, and "missing" looks the same as "unmounted" | KG "siblings"; CL | v4 lives under `$HOME` (A2). The `host-path` reflex stays |
| `/tmp` is tmpfs: leftovers occupy RAM, and the device rule refuses tmpfs | KG §4; DR:1760 | No state, backup or worktree in `/tmp`. Disposable HOMEs go under `~/.cache/hee4-host/<run>/` (FC1:163) |
| A shared `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` runs the **other** worktree's binary | memory `per-worktree-target-dir` | One target per worktree, derived from the worktree path by `tools/gate`, never exported globally |
| cargo-mutants with an inherited `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` links the unmutated lib, which voids the whole run | CL gate 3; F118 | `tools/mutants` **unsets** it and refuses to start if it is set. A planted surviving-mutant control proves the run mutated |
| Builds on the spindle wedge ext4 | CL gate 3; F111 | All targets on the NVMe (`~/.cache`); the STORAGE-10TB disk holds only backups |
| Orphans from toolbox shells are adopted by conmon | KG §1 | serve lives only as a systemd unit. Tests become subreapers and stop children by process group |
| SIGHUP when a tab closes kills a `serve` started by hand | KG §6 | serve handles SIGHUP like SIGTERM (P3) and is started only by the unit |
| A pin digest is valid on one side only | KG §3 | The manifest stores **host** pins. HP-rows (host preconditions) re-read them on the host before every host run *(rev 2026-10-01, V2 X4)* |
| The daemon is not a descendant of its unit's MainPID | FC2:59-66 | Endpoint resolution by the LISTEN holder (P3); no unit or MainPID walk |
| A hand-typed reply fixture missed `context` | FC2:133-136 | Fixtures only from recordings (F113) |
| Host `python3` has `sqlite3` 3.51.2 | FC2:22 (H2-c) | Host read-only ledger reads stay `mode=ro` URIs |

