## 4 · Gate map

### 4.1 Tiers as v4 runs them

| Tier | When | What runs | Where | Prints (the verdict's input) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Tier-1** | per commit, about 5 min (NW:67-70) | targeted suites (a diff-scoped gate run prints **every skipped step with its reason**, *rev 2026-10-01, V4-17*); plants per rule under `--cap-lints=warn` with the **named killing test** required; open-code-review coverage pass; independent review on committed objects; scoped `cargo mutants` on store and policy changes | toolbox, the slice's own worktree | `plants=k/k killers=named`, `mutants caught=a survivors=b (each named or equivalent-with-reason)` |
| **Tier-2** | per stack of 3-6 slices (NW:71-72) | precount → the **full** `tools/gate` (never diff-scoped at a landing) + `tools/cold-clone` in parallel on the stack tip, at most 2 gates at once (the `hee3-gate` flock slots pattern) → land by fast-forward *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-17)* | toolbox | `steps=N matched=N tree=<sha> dirty=0` from **both**; the one-door census line `duplicate_sites=N` *(rev 2026-10-01, V4-17)* |
| **Host record** | per flow whose closure exists only on the host (RQ7-r2, DR:1737-1752) | a committed host test run through `flatpak-spawn --host`, with host preconditions HP0-HP9 (v3's P0-P9 rows; not phases, *rev 2026-10-01, V2 X4*) printed first, from a **clean main checkout**, against the `current` release | host | a committed record; the scoreboard **recomputes** the digest and prints `host=H` separately |
| **Tier-3** | per day and before any push (NW:73-74) | one publication cold clone at the push sha + `push-scan --control` + range scan + RA9 rows | toolbox | `cold steps=N matched=N`, `push-scan control=PASS lines=L hits=0`, `use=U bytes=B` |
| **Deployed aggregate** | at P7 and at every later release | `tools/check-deployed` over D1-D10 *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V7 F01: over D1–D9 at P7 and P8, printing `deployed=N/9`; over D1–D10 from P9 entry on)* | host reads | `deployed=N/10 … verdict=` (one unit; F138) |

### 4.2 v3 failure modes, and the mechanism that makes v4 immune

| v3 failure mode | Evidence | v4 mechanism (structural, not "remember to") |
|---|---|---|
| **Missing worktree inputs.** The gate copies a hand list (`quality_subject_paths()`), so a fixture present in the worktree was absent in the gate's copy and failed at clippy | memory `hee3-gate-declared-inputs` (gate-run `20260926T060950353320Z`) | Declared inputs = `git ls-files -z` at the gated sha, **plus** a committed list of fetched inputs by digest. The gate refuses an untracked file the build reads (a `strace`-free check: build in a `git archive` export) |
| **Cold clone reading the live checkout** (`sqlite-inputs` copied from REPO, and two scripts with two bundles) | A7 | One repo-owned `tools/cold-clone`. Every fetched input is named in `tools/offline-bundle.lock` with its sha256, and the clone refuses on mismatch |
| **Seam binaries.** A test-seam build able to reach production doors | DR:1760-1761 (OPS12 closure R1); RA1(b) DR:1521-1524 | Seams live only in `#[cfg(test)]` or in a separate test-only crate, never behind a feature flag on the product binary. `install-release` and D2 count `HEE3_TEST_`/`HEE4_TEST_` strings = 0, with a **positive control** over a real seamed binary (FC1:110-111) |
| **Stale host records** | RQ7-r2 cond. 3 (DR:1748); FC1:300-307 | Host status is computed: ancestor + no `src`/`Cargo`/`crates` diff + clean + digest recompute + `source_sha == manifest.source_commit`. A record never becomes a stored status. v3's 10 control cases are ported whole (FC1:316-327) |
| **Lint-killed plants.** A plant "killed" by a lint instead of a test | CLAUDE.md §3 (F133) | The plant battery runs with `--cap-lints=warn` and requires the named test in the failure. A compile-failure kill counts as a survivor |
| **Gate edited underneath** | memory `never-edit-a-gated-worktree` | worktree flock (the `hee3-gate` pattern) + the `gated-worktree-guard` reflex |
| **Load-induced reds read as defects** (180 s partition at 149-155 s; t21 timed out beside a build) | memory `no-builds-beside-a-gate`; DR:1828 | The gate records its step wall times and prints `margin=` per partition. The gate refuses to start while a foreign cargo process runs (census by exe, killing nothing) |
| **Leaked descendants** fail a green step | memory `gate-detects-leaked-descendants` | Kept (it is a real catch). Tests that spawn become subreapers and reap with `wait` under a budget (DR:1826) |
| **Restored plants with a kept mtime** run the stale mutant | memory `plant-restore-mtime-trap` | Restore by writing new bytes (not `copy2`), then `cargo clean -p <crate>` before the verdict |
| **Count pins drifting** (t25 "Ran N" in two places) | memory `hee3-gate-t25-count-pin` | Expectations are base-relative and derived (RA8, DR:1547-1551). No literal test counts |
| **A verdict naming no tree** | CLAUDE.md §4 (F126) | Every gate, cold-clone, host and deployed line carries `tree=<sha> dirty=N` |
| **Push by inference** | memory `push-needs-lukes-explicit-command` | Tier-3 **prepares** the push (scan, cold clone) and stops. The push runs only on Luke's literal word, read back with `ls-remote` |

