## 8 · Design set: per-module detail for the phase work *(rev 2026-10-01)*
Each phase builds the modules whose cards name it. The design detail for each module is in the v4 vault's [Module Design Index](obsidian://open?vault=herdr-engineering-engine-v4.vault&file=15%20Module%20Design%2F00%20-%20Module%20Design%20Index), and every card links its own section. The module × phase matrix and the development workflows DW-1…DW-7 are in `16 System Maps/Workflow and Loop Map`. The D-rows' read-back paths are traced in `End-to-End Flow Traces` (E2E-01…12). Size budgets are in `Anti-Bloat Budget`: v4.0 upper bound 41,150 lines, K6 split trigger at 35%. **Authority is unchanged:** this atlas and the ULTRAMAP win over the design notes. ~~The design conflicts DC-01…DC-22 that touch a phase gate are DC-01 (P3 check stage), DC-06/07 (P1 transition table), DC-17 (P4 release verbs) and DC-22 (P2 backup trigger). Each needs ratification (H-27) before its phase slice.~~ *(rev 2026-10-01 alignment: superseded; the register now carries a phase on every open row, and §9 lists them per phase, generated.)*

